            <ArticleTitle>A case of lethal giant inguinal hernia.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>301-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1002/ccr3.484</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Several elective surgical managements have been reported regarding giant inguinal hernias (GIH), but no case of death. We here present a fatal case of bilateral GIHs in an extremely obese man with dyspnea. Bilateral GIHs are difficult to recognize in extreme obesity. Moreover, operation is recommended when GIH is diagnosed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
